# Lines that may keep "conversation" (Sources/LoomCatalogUI, Sources/loom-app) or the word "Loom" (those two and
# LoomCore, LoomChat, LoomLaunchOptions, LoomRemora, LoomTerminal, loom-hook) inside a string literal. One extended
# regex per line, matched against the "path:line:code" text of the hit. Keep this short: evidence keys, identifiers
# and folder names only, never text the user reads.
# Development-evidence JSON keys (scripts parse them).
"conversationID"
"conversationTerminals"
# The data folders keep Loom's names (~/Library/Application Support/Loom and Loom-Dev, D-83).
dataDirectoryName
# A project's own name in the evidence banner's sample text, and Codex's `originator` value that sessions started by 1.7.0 and
# earlier carry (a data value read back from Codex, not a name the user reads).
CatalogModel\+EvidenceBanners\.swift:[0-9]+:.*“loom” is already in Sphyrna
CodexRoutingDiagnostics\.swift:[0-9]+:.*case "loom": "loom"
